From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 05:17:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(reconciliation): lock the payment set once a batch exists
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

sameFacts (used to decide whether a re-submission of an existing
batch_reference is a legitimate retry) only compares the three amount
totals, not paymentIds. A decision call (approve/reject) on an existing
variance batch could therefore supply a *different* set of payments than
the one originally submitted, as long as it summed to the same
recordedAmount. The INSERT into reconciliation_payments uses ON CONFLICT
DO NOTHING, which only skips exact duplicates, so the new set was added
ALONGSIDE the original instead of replacing it — the realized-charge
computation then summed every payment ever attached, silently including
payments nobody actually reviewed in that decision.

Reproduced live: submitted a batch with payment A (50,000), then approved
it supplying payments B+C (20,000+30,000, same total) instead. Both sets
ended up attached to the same reconciliation.

Fix: on any retry of an existing non-terminal batch (decision or otherwise),
the caller's paymentIds must be exactly the set already attached to that
reconciliation, order-independent. A mismatch throws
RECONCILIATION_PAYMENT_SET_MISMATCH before anything is inserted.

Adds two regression tests plus a seedPaidBranchInBranch() fixture helper
for seeding a second payment into an already-seeded branch/policy.
